Subject: [PATCH] unix: link the desktop build dynamically

The desktop binary used to be linked with -static ("all libraries included").
That cannot host ALSA: distros ship only libasound.so, and a statically linked
alsa-lib was measured to be unusable (its config parser spins inside a static
glibc binary, and without the plugin layer it can only take the sound card
exclusively, which fails next to PulseAudio/PipeWire). The desktop build is
linked normally now: libc and libasound come from the host, everything else
(SDL, LVGL, MicroPython, the engines) is still in the binary.

As a side effect this also fixes modffi's dlopen, which had the same
static-binary problem (a shared library ending up with a second copy of libc's
state).

--- a/builder/unix.py
+++ b/builder/unix.py
@@ -101,9 +101,6 @@
         ]
     )
 
-    if REAL_PORT == 'unix':
-        unix_cmd.append('LDFLAGS_EXTRA=-static')  # static binary (all libraries included) so it's more portable
-
     # unix_cmd.extend(extra_args)
 
     clean_cmd.extend(unix_cmd[:])
